      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell>Number of pods per node</TableCell>
      <TableCell>2,500</TableCell>
      <TableCell>This was tested on a cluster with 31 servers: 3 control planes, 2 infrastructure nodes, and 26 compute nodes. If you need 2,500 user pods, you need both a <code>hostPrefix</code> of <code>20</code>, which allocates a network large enough for each node to contain more than 2000 pods, and a custom kubelet config with <code>maxPods</code> set to <code>2500</code>. For more information, see <a href="https://cloud.redhat.com/blog/running-2500-pods-per-node-on-ocp-4.13">Running 2500 pods per node on OCP 4.13</a>.</TableCell>
